WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Hello both, thanks for jumping on. So, I've got news on Willowmere Cottage.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.200
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Oh God, okay, is it good news?

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.667
<v Matthias Szymanski>Let him talk, love.

00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:16.867
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Ha. It's mixed. So the vendors have come back on your offer.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.467
<v Matthias Szymanski>Right.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:24.867
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>You offered $842K. They've said they'd accept, um, a bit more. They want 684k.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:28.533
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>That's, what, like four percent more?

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:31.600
<v Matthias Szymanski>Bit under. Three and a half.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:41.867
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>About that, yes. And, between us, I think they'll go lower, they're going through a divorce and they need it sold before the court date.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:47.333
<v Matthias Szymanski>Ah. um, That's, um. That's useful to know. Bit grim, but useful.

00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:49.867
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>I didn't say um, it.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.933
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Say what? Ha.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:57.467
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Ha. Exactly. So, how are you both feeling about the house itself?

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:05.600
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>I love I mean, it. I love it. The I mean, garden, the little shed, the view over to the Malvern Hills...

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Matthias Szymanski>The survey's what uh, worries me.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:17.467
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Yes. So the surveyor flagged some uh, damp in the back bedroom, and the roof's, um, got maybe ten years left.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.333
<v Matthias Szymanski>And the subsidence thing.

00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:25.800
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Historic. Historic subsidence. It's been monitored, it's stable.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.733
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>What does that mean for, like, insurance?

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:40.600
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Premiums can be like, a bit higher. Maybe fifteen to twenty percent above normal. Hartfield Mutual are usually decent for um, that sort of thing.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.800
<v Matthias Szymanski>Okay. And the mortgage? We're with Kingsmead Building Society in principle.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.867
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>What rate did they give you?

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.467
<v Matthias Szymanski>4% fixed, five years.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:02:00.533
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>That's good. That's really uh, good, actually. I've like, seen people at five and a quarter this month.

00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:04.400
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>We put down ten percent. Is that enough?

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:10.000
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>For that rate, yes. I mean, More is always better, but ten's fine.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:21.933
<v Matthias Szymanski>We were going to put down more, but my company's just announced a restructure and I don't know yet whether I've got a job in January, so we're keeping some back.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.067
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Very sensible.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:30.867
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>We're also, um, selling the place like, in Embleside Heath. My flat. Well, our flat.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.933
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Oh, right, how's that going?

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:41.667
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Slowly. The buyer's mortgage fell through because apparently he lied about his income, which, wow.

00:02:41.867 --> 00:02:45.533
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Oof. That happens more than you'd think.

00:02:45.733 --> 00:02:50.000
<v Matthias Szymanski>Can I ask about basically, the area? The schools?

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:58.000
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Sure. Primary's rated outstanding, in the village. Secondary is the one in Marston Rue, which is fine.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.867
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>And crime?

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:05.733
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Very low. The only thing anyone complains about is the bypass traffic.

00:03:05.933 --> 00:03:10.267
<v Matthias Szymanski>And there's no plans to build on the field behind?

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:20.600
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Not that I know of. I'd check with the council though, between us the farmer who owns it has been quietly talking to a housing developer.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.867
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Ooh. Neighbours!

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.933
<v Matthias Szymanski>Not helpful, you know, love.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:30.667
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Ha. So, what would you like me to say to the vendors?

00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:35.867
<v Matthias Szymanski>Let's say $313K, and we can complete by the end of February.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:40.800
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Can we say mid-February? I want to be in by Valentine's.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.333
<v Matthias Szymanski>That's not how it basically, works.

00:03:44.533 --> 00:03:52.867
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Ha. I'll say end of February, with flexibility. I mean, And I'll push uh, the damp as a reason for the number.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.400
<v Matthias Szymanski>Good.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.533
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Can I just get your solicitor's details again for the memo?

00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:08.800
<v Matthias Szymanski>Yes, it's Penrose Fairclough, and the contact is Ottilie Treadwell. basically, Her email is lmerriweather@corrimond.test.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.467
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Lovely. basically, And sort of, best number for you?

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.667
<v Matthias Szymanski>(253) 555-0130.

00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:19.733
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Or mine, I always pick up! +1 524 555 0116.

00:04:19.933 --> 00:04:26.733
<v Ilsabet Nakashima-Ford>Ha, noted. Okay, I'll come back sort of, to you by tomorrow afternoon. Fingers crossed.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.067
<v Peregrina Gilchrist-Mohr>Fingers and toes!

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.067
<v Matthias Szymanski>Thanks. Bye.
